adapted to catch upon the head of a bolt or a nut, or to hold a metal pipe or rod, so as to turn it. {{smaller|Some wrenches have a variety of jaws to suit different sizes and shapes of nuts and bolts, and others, as the monkey-wrench, have an adjustable inner jaw.}} —'''6†.''' Means of compulsion. [Rare.]
{{smaller block|He . . . resolved to make his profit of this businesse . . . of Naples as a ''wrench'' and meane for peace.
